.fill.justify.offset 5.rightmargin 55.pagesize 48.m1 2.m2 1.m3 2.m4 3.ec \.header /Sysinfo/OS9Lib/Sysinfo.footer /Page #//Printed (%)/.in +5.define topic.bold.in -5$1 $2 $3 $4 $5.in +5.en.define endtopic.en.define noform.nojustify.nofill.en.define noformend.justify.fill.en.! Manual created with MWB.! END-OF-MACRO.topic NAMESysinfo - Access the system-wide Parameters.endtopic.topic SYNOPSIS.noformint	info_type (name)char	*name;char	*info_str (name, str, len)char	*name;char	*str;int	len;int	info_num(name)char	*name;int	info_is_locked (name)char	*name;int	info_lock (name, signal)char	*name;int	signal;int	info_unlock (name)char	*name;int	info_change (name, signal)char	*name;int	signal;int	info_signal (name)char	*name;int	info_kill (name)char	*name;.noformend.endtopic.topic DESCRIPTION	The.ulSysinfoconcept is completly new for OS9. Designed by TOP Munich andwritten by Wolfgang Ocker, this concept provides the possibility to holdsystem wide information in a global data module and allows the lockingof abstract `devices` like uucp etc. To access this module thereexist various functions.	The function.ulinfo_type()accepts a string and determines the kind of the entry `name`..ulinfo_str()needs a string with the name of an entry, a pointer to abuffer where the result will be copied to and the size of the buffer. Itextracts the string of the entry defined by the name and copies thefound entry into the buffer..ulinfo_num()accepts a name and returns the value of the entry..ulinfo_is_locked()needs a string as an argument and returns the status of the given entry:locked by another process or free..ulinfo_lockneeds two arguments, the first is the name of an entry, the second is asignal number which should be send to the process when anotherone tries to lock the entry. When the locking process receives thatsignal, it can clean up everything and then release the lock. If the signalnumber in the entry is -1, the locking process doesn't want to releasethe device. No signal should be sent to such a process (info_lockhandles this correctly.).ulinfo_unlock()allows to unlock an entry previous locked by this process. With.ulinfo_change()the signal number can be changed. This may be necassary during criticalsections..ulinfo_signal()sends the specified signal to the process locking the named entry..ulinfo_kill()sends the specified signal + 1 to the process locking the named entry..endtopic.topic RETURN VALUEInfo_type returns the type of the entry on success, -1 on failure. Info_str returns a pointer to the buffer on success, NULL on failure. Info_num returns the value of the entry on success, -1 on failure. Info_is_locked, info_lock, info_unlock, info_change, info_signal andinfo_kill return 0 on success and -1 on failure..endtopic.topic SEE ALSO.noformSysinfo, Setup, Getinfoin the TOP Munich Release.noformend.endtopic